<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pakistan's jailed former PM Khan's sons told DW the authorities are cracking down ahead of new PTI protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79252b87238ff9129cef088afbaaadf00df9b59c23236315cfb8d0800e351e79</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-jailed-former-pm-khan-s-sons-told-dw-the-authorities-are-cracking-down-ahead-of-new-pti-p/a-79392147--8ea0d4621d28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-jailed-former-pm-khan-s-sons-told-dw-the-authorities-are-cracking-down-ahead-of-new-pti-protests/a-79392147?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sons of jailed Pakistani ex-PM Imran Khan told DW their father is in ill-health while being isolated from family and doctors. Other family members have been detained ahead of a planned opposition protest.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Slovakia: PM Robert Fico's NATO Article 5 remarks spark criticism and raise questions about his country's NATO commitment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:480b5029c7b5a109c8aba30e26e51bbbec8d0de45e204a2b02aaac626c9df87e</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-count/a-79387050--e3e0d18cd9d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-country-s-nato-commitment/a-79387050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico says he fears war and will do everything he can to keep his country out of one. Critics say his remarks risk weakening NATO, the alliance that was designed to prevent such a war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's oldest party, the center-left SPD, is in a difficult position following its success in the Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77062f94761105e51a42e3d13ed2e7bd2b968d10b7a94ea048bc6b34041a2880</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-m/a-79376827--2a4f42a68594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-state-election/a-79376827?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz (CDU) has vowed to press ahead with controversial reforms, but resistance is mounting within his coalition partner, the SPD. How much dissent can a governing coalition tolerate?</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Fighting resumes in Tigray</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b7beaa94fc47664ab849e37b8720d344f9ec5483ce66397713ffc12892eec3b</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-fighting-resumes-in-tigray/a-79394192--9abf0a9cd5c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-fighting-resumes-in-tigray/a-79394192?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rebels in northern Ethiopia have seized regional airports and engaged government troops in Afar and Amhara. Observers fear deadly clashes could expand after rebels announced a new anti-government alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>ICC convicts CAR ex-rebel leader of crimes against humanity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a742e734f19289168e49b8b026d48e072ba09e10710435eda58e78b6bdc3cc0e</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icc-convicts-car-ex-rebel-leader-of-crimes-against-humanity/a-79387178--62b2a3b09a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icc-convicts-car-ex-rebel-leader-of-crimes-against-humanity/a-79387178?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court has found Mahamat Said Abdel Kani guilty of overseeing torture and other crimes. He headed a feared prison unit that held political prisoners.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As the EU advances free trade with Southeast Asia, why is there no ASEAN-wide deal?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ea147652c5f4394c9255ca12d5c6530c18a10396eaa4e744c211570a8680054</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-the-eu-advances-free-trade-with-southeast-asia-why-is-there-no-asean-wide-deal/a-79388278--5f329cf78840.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-the-eu-advances-free-trade-with-southeast-asia-why-is-there-no-asean-wide-deal/a-79388278?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of arduous negotiations, the EU is closing on a string of bilateral trade deals with countries in Southeast Asia. And yet, a bloc-to-bloc agreement between the EU and ASEAN remains a distant prospect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Munich, Berlin, Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr – Germany's three Olympic candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2b5c42cfee653559a88fd620a22f763331f97b9586bee9f8a2e8f56a04abf77</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-berlin-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-three-olympic-candidates/a-79386915--56e9e5ef3aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-berlin-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-three-olympic-candidates/a-79386915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich, Berlin, or the Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr region? Germany aims to host the Olympic Games again. Three candidates are in the running, with one city considered the slight favorite.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Rome's Colosseum closes after worker falls to his death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dc73cb00821fba756bb442f227a078f773f62b0cb960bc6eb3b55dcda8861ff</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rome-s-colosseum-closes-after-worker-falls-to-his-death/a-79387180--030a6ce0cdab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rome-s-colosseum-closes-after-worker-falls-to-his-death/a-79387180?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man had been working on a new lighting installation in the iconic Roman amphitheater. Italian authorities said they were working on determining the circumstances of the accident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary: EU Commission wants to unblock €4.2b in funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c201d3aa4732a0d725fb59b3a58b4a5ba349334c6f60da0421047d4dbfe0fc19</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eu-commission-wants-to-unblock-_4-2b-in-funding/a-79386848--1c819fc4fb27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eu-commission-wants-to-unblock-€4-2b-in-funding/a-79386848?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Commission's president has argued that Budapest is strengthening the rule of law with Viktor Orban finally out of office. Funds had been blocked over corruption allegations under Hungary's former government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>OECD says growth 'resilient' in 2026 despite Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6990f83bc108db4926054b717428338890d6b543fa2cae63e6335b6e11acabf7</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oecd-says-growth-resilient-in-2026-despite-middle-east-war/a-79386625--7b0c955491ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oecd-says-growth-resilient-in-2026-despite-middle-east-war/a-79386625?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The OECD group of industrialized nations put its 2026 growth forecast at 2.9%. It said investment in AI was helping drive growth, while the war in the Middle East was fueling inflation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Campus Project 2026: Georgia Takes Center Stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79d89fb81422ea298864a84d8dfaf5e81dd1d61425bf851ab808854a50cc3f7f</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639--efaea8063cd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Beethovenfest exchange project brings German and Georgian musical traditions together. And the reasons go beyond music.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino explained: How the weather pattern affects hurricanes and tropical storms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeb4d52698c918b0e0eb19ec1da25ce3e0bafd9e265db64e36051ea3dd29011</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511--be7cc5c8c0e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From drought to major floods and extreme heat, El Nino will have a huge impact on the world's weather. In the Atlantic, it could mean a season without hurricanes.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UNGA: World leaders discuss AI, global conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unga-world-leaders-discuss-ai-global-conflicts/live-79366211--1636008645b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unga-world-leaders-discuss-ai-global-conflicts/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the UN General Assembly starts its second day, much attention will turn to the war in Iran, artificial intelligence and climate change. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's new travel rules unsettle tech giants and talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c540b6bb39a0864ac79e5ba1b09a2a33162db87a8456b198d599b4b7b9927c2c</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937--16d904ca4025.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing is locking the gates to stop expertise and capital in strategic industries from fleeing. The country accused of industrial-scale intellectual property theft now fears the West will take its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Famine threatens the Ukrainian town of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region as Russia delays creating a humanitarian evacuation corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d3f8f4621087f9f11946402066d2ceecd5764f98fc66e60f54266ed83fa8a35</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creat/a-79380887--1d1c80d27c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creating-a-humanitarian-evacuation-corridor/a-79380887?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Food supplies to the town of Oleshky in the occupied part of the southern Kherson region have been cut off since May. Efforts by Kyiv to negotiate the evacuation of civilians with Moscow have been largely unsuccessful.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>World lagging on key UN biodiversity targets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:120b0faba7a23f00435bb84b139f06a6f24f2ebcaf2fe49ecab22f32cc1990f9</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T07:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-lagging-on-key-un-biodiversity-targets/a-79383304--007a9149730c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-lagging-on-key-un-biodiversity-targets/a-79383304?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of nations signed on to a goal to protect 30% of the world's land and sea by 2030. As the timeline reaches the halfway point, activists say the current protection estimates are way behind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Call to scrap once-a-day gas price rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:025777e8d8b8596fe7fbebf29d5e14a5a0f8549a3c312aaa4ae90fab70707857</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523--75528f1f86f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ADAC motoring association says a once-a-day rule on gas price changes has failed to help drivers' wallets. Entry-level jobs are becoming scarcer, making things hard for those entering the job market. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: El Nino heat could kill 15,800 by February, report warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ede8a274fae98eb0f012d4ec272df9434d5964c6a1ca6802dee24b052e761cc</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-heat-could-kill-15-800-by-february-report-warns/live-79382508--7338ab67b490.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-heat-could-kill-15-800-by-february-report-warns/live-79382508?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Climate Impact Lab report warned that the El Nino heat will be most dangerous in places that are already hot and relatively poor. Meanwhile, Canada says PM Modi just confirmed a trip to the nation. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Syria's 'new' economy for the rich only?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd7f45b4fbb63d0c7875c43d294e54bf33f34d0971b8525e6158f70bd2cc7316</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T06:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-syria-s-new-economy-for-the-rich-only/a-79378442--fca620d74167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-syria-s-new-economy-for-the-rich-only/a-79378442?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Syrian government says it is restructuring the economy and announces prosperity. But ordinary Syrians are not feeling it. In fact, they say their lives are getting worse. Who exactly is likely to benefit then?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: 11 killed in attack on house party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7d4df011d6473f23807e4efeca495414ba08b562d5094843f371212390b4af7</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-11-killed-in-attack-on-house-party/a-79382743--e4b1a2c13c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-11-killed-in-attack-on-house-party/a-79382743?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motive for the shooting in the town of KwaMakhutha near Durban, Kwa-Zulu Natal was not immediately clear. Some of the victims were known to police</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: 15 men jailed for life in 2019 Easter bombings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6eca1fd13bf282d32d61175fd33d80f1aa2b545cd50aa7ab6d5f269ff9a84cc7</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T05:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-15-men-jailed-for-life-in-2019-easter-bombings/a-